  "count": 3,
  "rationale": "Block browserStore:credentialAccess, printServer:lateralMovement and backupHost:lateralMovement. Why this cut works: (1) browserStore is the only route to appServer, because dbLogin and vpnSession both require browserStore. It is also a required parent of dbLogin, so blocking it kills dbLogin, domainAdmin, dbReplica and appServer. (2) printServer is a required parent of hypervisor, so blocking it kills hypervisor. With appServer, domainAdmin and hypervisor gone, codeRepo is unreachable, and printServer's own route to shareMount is also closed. (3) Blocking backupHost kills serviceAccount and secretsManager, which closes the remaining routes to shareMount and vaultRead. All four parents of crownData are then unreachable. Why fewer than 3 is impossible: there are three attack routes that share no blockable step. Route 1: phishing -> browserStore -> appServer -> codeRepo. Route 2: vpnGateway -> tokenCache -> printServer -> shareMount. Route 3: supplychain -> iotDevice/memoryDump -> ssoLogin -> backupHost, together with exposedApi -> sshKey -> jumpHost, feeding secretsManager -> vaultRead. Each route reaches the target on its own, so any single blocked step can stop at most one of them."
 },
